|Working visit. Meeting with the President of Suriname, [[Chan Santokhi]], and the President of [[Guyana]], [[Irfaan Ali]]. Signed cooperation agreements for exploration of new Guyanese and Surinamese reserves of gas and oil by [[Petrobras]].<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://newsroom.gy/2021/12/18/massive-regional-summit-to-be-held-here-aluminium-plant-possible-for-berbice/|title=Massive regional summit to be held here; aluminium plant possible for Berbice|date=December 18, 2021|access-date=December 31, 2021|archive-date=December 20, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211220160448/https://newsroom.gy/2021/12/18/massive-regional-summit-to-be-held-here-aluminium-plant-possible-for-berbice/|url-status=live}}</ref>
|-
|rowspan=2|20
|15–17 February
|{{flagu|Russia}}
|[[Moscow]]
|State visit. President Bolsonaro was invited by [[Vladimir Putin]] to a Russia-Brazil summit at Kremlin, amid tension with the US and NATO over Ukraine. Discussion about the global geopolitical situation and tension in Europe, cooperation in defense for technology for cyber security and combat systems for UAVs. Russia formally supports a permanent seat for Brazil in the UN Security Council. Bolsonaro also visits the [[State Duma]] and meet with the Duma's Chairman [[Vyacheslav Volodin]].<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.gov.br/mre/en/contact-us/press-area/press-releases/joint-statement-by-president-of-the-federative-republic-of-brazil-jair-bolsonaro-and-president-of-the-russian-federation-vladimir-putin|title=Joint Statement by President of the Federative Republic of Brazil Jair Bolsonaro and President of the Russian Federation Vladimir Putin|date=February 16, 2022|website=gov.br/mre|access-date=February 16, 2022|archive-date=February 16, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220216173505/https://www.gov.br/mre/en/contact-us/press-area/press-releases/joint-statement-by-president-of-the-federative-republic-of-brazil-jair-bolsonaro-and-president-of-the-russian-federation-vladimir-putin|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=http://en.kremlin.ru/events/president/news/67770|title=On February 16, Vladimir Putin will hold talks with President of Brazil Jair Bolsonaro|date=February 16, 2022|website=Kremlin.ru|access-date=February 15, 2022|archive-date=February 15, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220215120835/http://en.kremlin.ru/events/president/news/67770|url-status=live}}</ref>
|-
|17 February
|{{flagu|Hungary}}
|[[Budapest]]
|State visit. Meeting with the Prime Minister [[Viktor Orban]], President [[János Áder]] and the [[National Assembly (Hungary)|National Assembly]] Chairman [[László Kövér]].<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://oglobo.globo.com/mundo/bolsonaro-chega-russia-no-auge-da-tensao-com-agenda-restrita-1-25392920|title=Bolsonaro chega à Rússia no auge da tensão e com agenda restrita|date=February 14, 2022|website=O Globo|language=pt|access-date=February 14, 2022|archive-date=February 14, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220214104911/https://oglobo.globo.com/mundo/bolsonaro-chega-russia-no-auge-da-tensao-com-agenda-restrita-1-25392920|url-status=live}}</ref>
|-
|21
|6 May
|{{flagu|Guyana}}
|[[Georgetown, Guyana|Georgetown]]
|State visit. Meeting with President [[Irfaan Ali]]. Addressed bilateral issues between Brazil and Guyana in the areas of trade, oil, economy, infrastructure and electricity.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.correiodopovo.com.br/not%C3%ADcias/pol%C3%ADtica/bolsonaro-vai-%C3%A0-guiana-discutir-importa%C3%A7%C3%B5es-petr%C3%B3leo-e-fibra-%C3%B3tica-1.817470|title=Bolsonaro vai à Guiana discutir importações, petróleo e fibra ótica|date=6 May 2022 |access-date=June 7, 2022|archive-date=June 8, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220608163545/https://www.correiodopovo.com.br/not%C3%ADcias/pol%C3%ADtica/bolsonaro-vai-%C3%A0-guiana-discutir-importa%C3%A7%C3%B5es-petr%C3%B3leo-e-fibra-%C3%B3tica-1.817470|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=http://noticias.r7.com/jr-na-tv/videos/em-viagem-a-guiana-bolsonaro-chama-petrobras-de-gigante-brasileira-06052022|title=Página não encontrada - Portal R7|work=R7.com |date=6 May 2022 |access-date=June 7, 2022|archive-date=May 7, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220507073826/https://noticias.r7.com/jr-na-tv/videos/em-viagem-a-guiana-bolsonaro-chama-petrobras-de-gigante-brasileira-06052022|url-status=live}}</ref>
|-
|22
|9–11 June
|{{flagu|United States}}
|[[Los Angeles]], [[Orlando, Florida|Orlando]]
|Working visit. In [[Los Angeles]], the President attended the [[Summit of the Americas]] and had a bilateral meeting with [[President of the United States|President]] [[Joe Biden]]. The President also met with Colombian president [[Iván Duque]], with Ecuadorian president [[Guillermo Lasso]] and with Dominican president [[Luis Abinader]]. In [[Orlando, Florida|Orlando]], Bolsonaro participated in the inauguration of the Brazilian vice consulate in the city.<ref>{{cite web | url=https://blogs.oglobo.globo.com/lauro-jardim/post/bolsonaro-aceita-se-reunir-com-biden.html | title=Bolsonaro aceita se reunir com Biden | date=25 May 2022 | access-date=June 7, 2022 | archive-date=May 25, 2022 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220525220705/https://blogs.oglobo.globo.com/lauro-jardim/post/bolsonaro-aceita-se-reunir-com-biden.html | url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite web | url=https://valor.globo.com/politica/noticia/2022/06/03/aps-cpula-das-amricas-bolsonaro-ir-a-orlando.ghtml | title=Após Cúpula das Américas, Bolsonaro irá a Orlando | date=3 June 2022 | access-date=June 7, 2022 | archive-date=June 8, 2022 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220608090220/https://valor.globo.com/politica/noticia/2022/06/03/aps-cpula-das-amricas-bolsonaro-ir-a-orlando.ghtml | url-status=live }}</ref>
|-
|23
|31 August
|{{flagu|Paraguay}}
|[[Brazil–Paraguay border]]
|Working visit. President Bolsonaro met with [[President of Paraguay]], [[Mario Abdo Benítez]] to make a technical visit over the Jaime Lerner bridge, which connects the cities of [[Foz do Iguaçu]] and [[Ciudad del Este]]. He briefly crossed the border line to the Paraguayan side.<ref>{{cite web | url=https://aldianews.com/en/politics/policy/brazil-paraguay-celebrate | title=Brazil and Paraguay celebrate integration on the new binational bridge | access-date=September 1, 2022 | archive-date=September 1, 2022 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220901045020/https://aldianews.com/en/politics/policy/brazil-paraguay-celebrate | url-status=live }}</ref>
|-
|rowspan=2|24
|18–19 September
|{{flagu|United Kingdom}}
|[[London]]
|State visit. President Bolsonaro went to the [[Palace of Westminster]], where the funeral of [[Monarchy of the United Kingdom|Queen]] [[Elizabeth II]] was taking place. Had a meeting with the new [[Monarchy of the United Kingdom|King]] of the United Kingdom [[Charles III]], meeting at [[Buckingham Palace]], with other Heads of State Government. Attended the state funeral of Queen Elizabeth II in [[Westminster Abbey]] magazine with [[First Lady of Brazil|First Lady]] [[Michelle Bolsonaro]]. Both were received for a meeting by the [[Secretary of State for Foreign, Commonwealth and Development Affairs]] and UK Minister [[James Cleverly]].<ref>{{cite web | url=https://www.cnnbrasil.com.br/internacional/bolsonaro-visita-o-caixao-e-presta-homenagem-a-rainha-em-londres/ | title=Bolsonaro visita o caixão e presta homenagem à rainha, em Londres | date=18 September 2022 | access-date=September 18, 2022 | archive-date=September 18, 2022 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220918131933/https://www.cnnbrasil.com.br/internacional/bolsonaro-visita-o-caixao-e-presta-homenagem-a-rainha-em-londres/ | url-status=live }}</ref>
|-
|20 September
|rowspan=2|{{flagu|United States}}
|[[New York City]]
|Working visit. President Bolsonaro will deliver the traditional opening address of the [[United Nations General Assembly]].<ref>{{cite web | url=https://www.cnnbrasil.com.br/politica/na-onu-bolsonaro-nao-deve-se-reunir-com-biden-e-outros-lideres-de-potencias-mundiais/ | title=Na ONU, Bolsonaro não deve se reunir com Biden e outros líderes de potências mundiais | date=17 September 2022 | access-date=September 18, 2022 | archive-date=September 17, 2022 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220917213631/https://www.cnnbrasil.com.br/politica/na-onu-bolsonaro-nao-deve-se-reunir-com-biden-e-outros-lideres-de-potencias-mundiais/ | url-status=live }}</ref>
|-
|25
|30 December
|[[Florida]]
|President Bolsonaro travelled Florida to avoid the inauguration to his successor, [[Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva]], who defeated him in the [[2022 Brazilian general election]]. 
